# Skills the desk gets, on top of the pinned Anthropic office set in the image.
#
# `make desk-skills` copies each of these out of ~/.claude/skills (following
# the symlinks into ~/.agents/skills) into ai-deck/skills/, which is
# bind-mounted read-only at /opt/user-skills and linked into ~/.claude/skills
# by entrypoint.sh. Add a line, run the target, deploy.
#
# Two rules for what belongs here: it has to work inside the container (no
# browser, no display server, no age key, no NAS SSH key), and it has to be
# for the work the desk is for — documents and thinking, not editing this
# repo. See scripts/desk_skills.py for why this is an allowlist.

# House style. The caveman hook is on in every session, so the desk should be
# able to answer /caveman-help and /caveman-stats like the workstation does.
caveman
caveman-help
caveman-review
caveman-stats
caveman-commit
caveman-compress
cavecrew

# Diagrams. validate + deliver are pure Node and work here; visual-check
# looks for a system chrome binary the image does not have, so it will report
# an environmental failure rather than browser evidence.
archify

# Thinking and shaping, before anything gets written.
brainstorming
grilling
prototype
research
writing-plans

# Turning a pile of notes into a document — the desk's actual job.
to-prd
to-spec
to-issues
to-tickets
to-questionnaire
teach
triage
wizard

# Writing craft.
writing-shape
writing-beats
writing-fragments

# Working on skills and agent-facing docs from the phone.
writing-skills
writing-for-agents
writing-great-skills

# Vocabulary and finishing.
domain-modeling
verification-before-completion
handoff
retro
